What:		/sys/bus/spi/devices/spi<bus>.<cs>/pen_scan
Date:		September 2026
KernelVersion:	7.2
Contact:	linux-input@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Reading returns whether the NT36536 touchscreen controller
		has been asked to scan for an active pen, 0 or 1.  Writing a
		boolean turns pen scanning on or off.  The default is off:
		scanning costs power and the controller does not report the
		pen without it.  The setting survives the firmware reload
		that follows every panel power up.

		The attribute only exists when the devicetree declares
		novatek,pen-support.

		Access: Read, Write

		Valid values: Boolean
